THIRD-PARTY GAMES AND CONTENT
====================================================================================================

Every game below, its names, pictures and data belong to the companies listed with it. This project
is an unofficial fan project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them, nor by the
services named as a source.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POKÉMON
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Owners
  Nintendo, Game Freak and The Pokémon Company.

Their content
  Pokémon names, images, sprites and related game content are their trademarks.

External links
  Links to external services such as Pokémon Showdown point to their own content.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WORLD OF WARCRAFT: FOREVER
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Owner
  Blizzard Entertainment, Inc. World of Warcraft names, icons, game data, game text and forum posts
  belong to Blizzard Entertainment, Inc.

Game data (talents, spellbooks, racials, professions and the Legacy System)
  Source: the tables of the World of Warcraft: Forever and Classic Era game clients, as wago.tools
  (https://wago.tools) publishes them for every game build.
  Use: the backend only reads the tables it needs and keeps one generated copy in its own private
  storage; it does not republish the game files. The web app credits the source on every page that
  uses the data.

Launcher news
  Source: the public RSS feed of Wowhead (https://www.wowhead.com/news/rss/forever).
  Use: the app only shows the title, the short summary, the date and the picture of each item, as
  the feed publishes them, with a link to the full article on Wowhead and a "Fuente: Wowhead" credit;
  it never copies the articles. The pictures are loaded straight from Wowhead's servers and are not
  stored.
  Rights: Wowhead news, texts and pictures belong to Wowhead and their authors.

Launcher blue posts
  Source: the public Blizzard tracker of the official World of Warcraft forums
  (https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/groups/blizzard-tracker/activity/posts).
  Use: the app only shows the topic title, the author, the date and the short excerpt of each post,
  as the forums publish them, with a link to the full post on the forums and a "Fuente: Blizzard
  Forums" credit; it never copies the posts.

Icons
  Game icons are loaded straight from Blizzard's icon host. The race icons of the races screen and
  the camp item icons of the professions screen are loaded straight from Wowhead's icon servers
  (wow.zamimg.com), because Blizzard's host lacks some of them. None are stored, and they are game
  icons that belong to Blizzard Entertainment, Inc.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LEAGUE OF LEGENDS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Owner
  Riot Games, Inc.

Legal notice
  NTG System isn't endorsed by Riot Games and doesn't reflect the views or opinions of Riot Games or
  anyone officially involved in producing or managing Riot Games properties. Riot Games, and all
  associated properties are trademarks or registered trademarks of Riot Games, Inc.
  The League of Legends screen shows this notice.

Match history, ranks and profiles
  Source: the Riot Games API (https://developer.riotgames.com), with a personal key.
  Use: the backend keeps a small summary of each game of the players linked in this private group; it
  does not keep the full game files or republish them. The key never leaves the backend.

Names and icons of champions, items and summoner spells
  Source: Data Dragon, the static files of Riot Games (https://ddragon.leagueoflegends.com).
  Use: the backend reads the names once a day. The pictures are loaded straight from Riot's servers
  and are not stored.


